# Product initiatives (not migration PRs)

The numbered migration (PR1–PR5) is **closed and finished**. Do not plan, branch, document, or talk about new work as `PR 6`, `PR 7`, `PR X.Y`, or similar. Do not use global numbering to represent project progress.

Binexus develops by **product initiatives and capabilities** on the definitive architecture — not as a continuing architectural migration.

## Before proposing implementation

1. Name the **product initiative** explicitly (enough to understand the goal without any prior numbering).
2. Organize work by that initiative / feature, not by a migration sequence.
3. Use descriptive titles for plans and checkpoints tied to the capability.

## Naming

| Artifact | Format | Example |
| -------- | ------ | ------- |
| Branch | `feat/<capability-name>` | `feat/branch-device-auth` |
| Plan | `PLAN — <CAPABILITY>` | `PLAN — BRANCH DEVICE AUTHENTICATION` |
| Checkpoint | `CHECKPOINT — <CAPABILITY> <MILESTONE>` | `CHECKPOINT — BRANCH DEVICE AUTH PR READY` |
| Large initiative phases | `Phase N — <slice>` **inside** that initiative only | `Phase 1 — Contracts` |

Forbidden: `PLAN PR 6`, `CHECKPOINT PR 6.1`, `feat/pr6-…`, migration-style `PR X.Y` labels for new work.

## Documentation

- `docs/migration/` is reserved exclusively for historical artifacts of the completed PR1–PR5 migration. Do not add new capability plans or checkpoints there.
- New plans, checkpoints, and feature notes live under a path that reflects the capability (e.g. `docs/<capability>/`, or living areas under `docs/architecture/`, `docs/domains/`, etc. when that fits).
- Architecture decisions, plans, and checkpoints must be self-explanatory from the initiative name alone.

## Examples (good)

```text
PLAN — BRANCH DEVICE AUTHENTICATION
CHECKPOINT — BRANCH DEVICE AUTH IMPLEMENTATION
CHECKPOINT — BRANCH DEVICE AUTH PR READY
```

```text
PLAN — OFFLINE SALES ENGINE
Phase 1 — Contracts
Phase 2 — Persistence
Phase 3 — Sync
```
